# Line endings (Kevin 17 Nov 2026): every text file is LF in the repo and in the working tree, whatever core.autocrlf
# says. Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so without this a checkout writes CRLF, the release
# and the tools write LF, and git status calls the file modified with an empty diff. The repo itself is already LF
# throughout (nothing renormalised). padel-share-api scripts/eol-refresh.mjs rewrites a checkout made before this, once.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
